    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d576">

                <pb facs="0882" n="872" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg872"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">General Marshall to the Acting Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-08-28">August 28, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1406. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Acheson</hi>: Admiral Cooke and I have
                    discussed at length the matter set forth in your message relayed to me by
                    Colonel Carter.<anchor n="49" xml:id="d576-f1"/> I approved his plan which is
                    similar to the one apparently mentioned to you by the Secretary of Navy.<anchor
                        n="50" xml:id="d576-f2"/> Further than this I authorized Admiral Cooke to
                    begin turning over train convoys and bridge guards at an early date so as to
                    obligate national forces to assume these duties. This will accomplish a double
                    purpose.</p>
                <p>The Marines will be relieved of some of their present functions thus permitting
                    their concentration. At the same time this will require available national
                    forces recently arrived in Chinwangtao and due for Manchuria to dispose
                    southward instead of northward into Jehol and Manchuria which I am convinced
                    will arouse serious Communist reactions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>G. C. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
